{"id":"leetcode-3370","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Smallest Number With All Set Bits","summary":"Given a positive integer n, find the smallest integer x ≥ n whose binary representation consists solely of 1s.","statement":"Given a positive integer n, find the smallest integer x ≥ n whose binary representation consists solely of 1s.","constraints":["Find the smallest integer at least n whose binary representation contains only one bits.","The answer must have no zero between its most significant and least significant bits.","Return that integer."],"topics":["bit manipulation","math"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"smallest_all_set_bits_number","parameters":[{"name":"n","annotation":"int","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"int","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def smallest_all_set_bits_number(n: int) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def smallest_all_set_bits_number(n):\n    return (1<<n.bit_length())-1\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def smallest_all_set_bits_number(n):\n    return (1<<n.bit_length()+1)-1\n","def smallest_all_set_bits_number(n):\n    return (1<<n.bit_length())-2\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(1)","target_space_complexity":"O(1)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["An all-one-bit number with b bits equals 2^b-1.","Use n’s bit length to select the smallest possible width.","The mask (1<<b)-1 is at least n and has all b bits set.","Any shorter all-one mask is below n, proving minimality."],"editorial":"Any shorter all-one mask is below n, proving minimality.","tests":[{"id":"lc-3370-1","arguments":[5],"expected":7,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Five is binary 101; the next all-one-bit value is binary 111, or seven.","exp